The published edition carries upstream's skills and nothing of mine
==================================================================

Three skills here are mine, not upstream's: `browser-driving`, `reverse-engineering` and `with`. They were
written for this edition and they belong in the developer series, where they are still shipped. A
published build should be upstream's product with my platform work in it, not my working library.

This removes them and leaves the manifest empty, so the app lists only what upstream ships (the office
skills) and whatever the machine's own Hermes profiles provide.

